# Runtime artifacts — derived cache, rebuildable from vault/ at any time.
vault/.brain/
# Per-vault runtime dirs created by a test run against a fixture vault
# (writer.lock and friends) — never fixture content, never committed.
tests/fixtures/**/.brain/
# ADR-0003 Ruling 1: the ingestion drop zone (visible, unlike .brain/) —
# originals + extracted sources belong in raw/ once promoted; the inbox
# itself (and its _processing/_quarantine/_duplicate scratch dirs) is never
# indexed and never committed.
vault/inbox/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-embed/
.fastembed_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Frozen brain binaries (built per-arch into the workspace, never committed).
dist/
build/
# PyInstaller writes a stray *.spec at the repo root when invoked without one;
# ignore those, but KEEP the authored, version-controlled specs under packaging/.
/*.spec
!packaging/**/*.spec
# CAP-02: the COS capture corpus — real message bodies at MNPI. It lives under
# the host-private base (off the Cowork mount, outside any checkout), so this is
# belt-and-braces for an operator who points $BRAIN_INDEX_DIR inside a clone.
cos-corpus/
# The derived SQLite index lives under app-data, never in-repo, but ignore any
# stray local index/snapshot just in case.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# S10 derived real-corpus index (369M, regenerable) — never commit
_evidence/s10/brain-index/
_models/
.venv-export/

# Session build evidence + eval gold/run data — derived, regenerable, kept LOCAL.
# (Removed from the public repo; do not re-commit.)
_evidence/*
# s09 exception: the two committed evidence samples for the AUT-01/AUT-03 HTML
# brief/digest renderers — generated with the NEUTRAL FALLBACK overlay only
# (ADR-0003 Ruling e / ADR-0001 clean-room export; never real owner content).
!_evidence/s09/
_evidence/s09/*
!_evidence/s09/brief.html
!_evidence/s09/digest.html
# s10 exception (GRF-01): the one committed graphify build-artifact sample,
# generated from the synthetic/neutral fixture corpus only — never real
# owner content (ADR-0003 Ruling e / ADR-0001 clean-room export).
!_evidence/s10/
_evidence/s10/*
!_evidence/s10/graph.json
# s04/s05 eval-launch evidence: PID/timestamp/query-count metadata only,
# never owner content — same allowlist pattern as s09/s10 above.
!_evidence/eval/
_evidence/eval/*
!_evidence/eval/heartbeat.txt
!_evidence/eval/DONE
!_evidence/eval/capture.lock
# S01 (obs-recovery-2026-07) baseline report: synthetic-vault timings + generic
# error-string counts only, never real owner/vault content.
!_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/
_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/*
!_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/baseline.md
# S02: two-writer stress transcript, generic synthetic-vault content only.
!_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/lock-contention-stress.txt
# S03B (RB-02): kill-resume transcript, generic synthetic-vault content only.
!_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/kill-resume-proof.txt
# eval-ledger-power-fusion-residual-2026-08-09: the whole evidence tree is
# TRACKED — it holds the fixture-recovery snapshot and the once-only held-out
# claim ledger, whose only backup is the commit. Ledger audits, fingerprint
# manifests and metric tables only; never real owner/vault content.
!_evidence/eval-power/
!_evidence/eval-power/**
# anylang-query-variants-2026-08-09 (CON-01): the language-census readout —
# per-language COUNTS, gold-document verdicts keyed by QUERY ID, and grep/tool
# transcripts. No corpus paths, no document text, no query text; same content
# class as the committed s09 stratum audit, and the acceptance review reads it.
# Allowlisted FILE BY FILE on purpose: a later session's evidence in this tree
# has to be a deliberate decision, never one inherited from this line.
!_evidence/anylang/
_evidence/anylang/*
!_evidence/anylang/s03-census.txt
# s04 (MEA-01): the pre-registration, the measurement readout and the DERIVED
# population inventory. Metric tables, query IDs, strata and language codes
# only — no corpus path, no document title, no query text, no variant text.
# Deliberately NOT allowlisted beside them: s04-variant-leakage.txt, which
# prints real gold-document titles next to the query text they were checked
# against. It exists and is non-empty on disk for the evidence gate; it stays
# untracked on purpose, same posture as s02's family probe.
!_evidence/anylang/s04-PRE-REGISTRATION.md
!_evidence/anylang/s04-variant-readout.md
!_evidence/anylang/s04-population-inventory.json
eval/_expand/
eval/golden_set*.json
# s03 (PWR-01/PWR-02): the staged expansion draft. Same content class as
# golden_set.json — real corpus paths plus verbatim spans quoted out of MNPI
# meeting notes, audits and decks — so it never enters a commit either.
eval/golden-expansion-draft.json
# ...and its review sheet, which is the ONE exception to the force-tracked
# _evidence/eval-power/ tree below: the evidence contract requires a span
# quoted from each gold DOCUMENT, and that is exactly the "real owner/vault
# content" that tree forbids. Excluded rather than redacted into uselessness;
# consequence is that it has no commit backup and must be read from disk.
_evidence/eval-power/s03-expansion-review.md
# s09 (PT-01/PT-02): the Portuguese expansion draft and its review sheet, same
# content class and same reason as the two s03 lines above — real corpus paths
# plus verbatim spans quoted out of MNPI Portuguese meeting notes, deep-dive
# reports and legal analyses. Neither has a commit backup; s05 reads both from
# disk. The s09 STRATUM AUDIT (`s09-pt-stratum-audit.md`) is NOT listed here —
# it carries counts, verdicts and fixture paths only, so it stays tracked.
eval/golden-expansion-draft-pt.json
_evidence/eval-power/s09-pt-expansion-review.md
eval/qrels/
eval/reformulations.json
eval/runs/
# HYG-02: the score-time codename map. It carries the PRIVATE corpus's real
# names on one side of every entry, so it is exactly as sensitive as
# golden_set.json — never committed. Absent map == identity (see
# eval/path_normalize.py); the scorecard stamps which map it used.
eval/codename-map.json

# s04 full-corpus capture: multi-hour job output is a TEMP artifact promoted
# to eval/runs/s13-final.json by s05 only AFTER the DONE sentinel validates —
# never commit the in-flight partial.
.brain/eval-tmp/

# S10 live-vault migration workspace — MNPI corpus, never committed.
_workspace/

# Plan artifacts — internal (contain the codename + session IDs); never ship.
# Grill decision 2026-07-03: ignore the whole tree, not just runtime state.
_plans/
_plans_index.md

# plan-execute runtime state (auto-added by plan-builder)
_plans/*/.lock
_plans/*/_closeouts/
_plans/*/run.ndjson
_plans/*/run_state.json
_plans/*/HALT_NOTICE.txt
_archive/
.claude/eval-gates.json
# Step 0a real-corpus validation: kill-resume on a real-content subset —
# counts and timings only, no note content.
!_evidence/obs-recovery-2026-07/real-corpus-validation.txt
dist_build/

# s05 (PWR-03): the PRE-MERGE fixture snapshot. `_evidence/eval-power/**` is
# force-tracked, but these three files are byte copies of the private fixtures
# (real corpus paths), so the copies stay out of the commit while
# `manifest.txt` beside them — sha256s and counts only — stays tracked. That
# manifest is what proves the snapshot was taken before the merge; the copies
# are the local revert path, which is why they are copies and not a git ref.
_evidence/eval-power/s05-fixtures-pre-merge/golden_set.json
_evidence/eval-power/s05-fixtures-pre-merge/qrels.json
_evidence/eval-power/s05-fixtures-pre-merge/codename-map.json
# s04 (MEA-01): the PRE-VARIANT fixture snapshot, same rule and same reason —
# byte copies of the private fixtures stay out of the commit, `manifest.txt`
# beside them (sha256s and counts only) stays tracked and is what proves the
# snapshot was taken before the variants were written.
_evidence/eval-power/s04-fixtures-pre-variants/golden_set.json
_evidence/eval-power/s04-fixtures-pre-variants/qrels.json
_evidence/eval-power/s04-fixtures-pre-variants/codename-map.json
# s08 (EVL-01): the PRE-EXPANSION fixture snapshot, same rule and same reason as
# the two blocks above — byte copies of the private fixtures stay out of the
# commit, `manifest.txt` beside them (sha256s, byte counts and the proved
# restore command) stays tracked and is what shows the snapshot was taken
# before the expansion.
_evidence/eval-power/s08-fixtures-pre-expansion/golden_set.json
_evidence/eval-power/s08-fixtures-pre-expansion/qrels.json
_evidence/eval-power/s08-fixtures-pre-expansion/codename-map.json
# s08 (EVL-01): the authored expansion draft and its per-stratum source files.
# Same content class as `golden-expansion-draft.json` above — real corpus paths
# plus question text derived from MNPI meeting notes, audits, contracts and
# decks — so neither enters a commit. `eval/_expand/` is already excluded; this
# line covers the assembled draft that sits beside the fixtures.
eval/golden-expansion-draft-s08.json

# s10 (EVL-03): the RAW per-query captures. `_evidence/eval-power/**` is
# force-tracked, but these two files hold every arm's returned document keys
# for every query — 10,603 real corpus paths, the same content class as
# eval/runs/ and golden_set.json. They exist on disk so a reporting bug never
# costs a re-capture (`--from-runs`), and they stay untracked for the same
# reason those do. The AGGREGATE artifacts beside them (s10-train.json,
# s10-validate.json, s10-train-extra-contrasts.json) carry metric tables,
# strata, counts and fixture digests only — verified 0 corpus paths — and stay
# tracked.
_evidence/eval-power/s10-attempt-1/s10-train-runs.json
_evidence/eval-power/s10-attempt-1/s10-train-runs-shipped-valve-30s.json

# s10 (EVL-03): the pre-registration, the claim readout and its rendered
# one-pager. `_evidence/*` above excludes this directory wholesale, so the
# directory itself is re-included first (an excluded parent cannot be
# re-entered by a file pattern). Same allowlisting posture, and same
# confidentiality review, as s04's equivalents above: metric tables, arm
# names, strata, criteria and fixture digests only — verified 0 corpus paths,
# 0 document titles, 0 query text. Everything else under _evidence/invariants/
# stays untracked, exactly as s01-s09 left it.
!_evidence/invariants/
_evidence/invariants/*
!_evidence/invariants/s10-PRE-REGISTRATION.md
!_evidence/invariants/s10-claim-readout.md
!_evidence/invariants/s10-one-pager.html

# /plan-harden 2026-08-15: per-worktree test scope for the pytest-quality-v2 gate.
# Scratch, never committed — seven tier-3 members each write their own, and a
# committed copy would be an M5 merge conflict over a file with no content value.
.quality-v2-scope
